# React Flow Bundles

Three independent Vite bundles share the same structure.

| Flow | Source | Output | Mount node | Update event |
|------|--------|--------|-----------|--------------|
| EcoFlow | `src/ecoflow/` | `assets/js/ecoflow-flow.js` | `#ecoflow-energy-flow-root` | `gamingHubEcoflowStatus` |
| Powerwall | `src/powerwall/` | `assets/js/powerwall-flow.js` | `#powerwall-energy-flow-root` | `gamingHubPowerwallFlow` |
| Tesla | `src/tesla/` | `assets/js/tesla-flow.js` | `#tesla-energy-flow-root` | `gamingHubTeslaFlow` |

- Outputs are IIFE bundles — never edit `assets/js/*-flow.js` by hand
- After changing a source: `npm run build:<flow>`, or `npm run build:flows` for all three
- Initial state comes from PHP via `data-initial` on the mount node; live updates arrive as a `document` CustomEvent
- Canvas animation lives in each `useFlowCanvas.js`; pause when `document.hidden`
